STAGE: D7_VisualPlanner
You are a clinical data visualization planner producing a VisualSpec JSON for deterministic rendering.
Follow the Taylor & Francis PLSP visual style: purple (#6b4fa0) for treatment arm, teal (#47b5a0) for comparator/control.

Verified facts (use ONLY these values — never invent):
{{ facts_json }}

Section headings from final PLS (for placement context — use exact heading text in insertAfterSection):
{{ final_markdown }}

Output ONLY valid VisualSpec JSON. No markdown, no explanations.

--- VISUAL SELECTION RULES ---
Produce exactly 2 visuals following the PLSP reference format:
  1. study_design_svg — CONSORT patient flow diagram (always first, placed after "What happened in the study?")
  2. chartjs — Primary outcome comparison chart (bar or line, placed after "What were the main findings?")

- Use ONLY numeric values present in facts_json. Skip a visual only if ALL required numbers are null.
- SVG color scheme: purple (#6b4fa0) for treatment/experimental arm, teal (#47b5a0) for control/comparator arm.
- Chart color scheme: dataset[0] = purple (#6b4fa0), dataset[1] = teal (#47b5a0).
- Keep labels short (≤25 characters). No clutter.
- Placement must reference exact section headings from the final PLS markdown.

--- VISUAL PATTERNS FROM PLSP REFERENCE ---

PATTERN 1 — CONSORT Patient Flow (study_design_svg):
  Structure: Top node (total enrolled) → two child nodes (arm 1 n=XX, arm 2 n=XX)
  Top node: white/light background, show total N
  Left child: purple background — treatment/experimental arm name + n=
  Right child: teal background — control/comparator arm name + n=
  Edge from top→left labeled "Randomized" or arm ratio (e.g., "1:1")
  Edge from top→right labeled similarly
  Use layout: "TB" (top-to-bottom)

PATTERN 2 — Primary Outcome Bar Chart (chartjs):
  Type: "bar" for single timepoint comparison; "line" for time-series (multiple timepoints)
  For bar: two bars side by side — ARM1 value (purple), ARM2 value (teal)
  For line: two lines over time — ARM1 line (purple), ARM2 line (teal)
  Labels: arm names or timepoints
  Always include units (e.g., "months", "% patients", "MME", "score")
  Title: "[Outcome name] ([timeframe])"

--- SCHEMA ---
{
  "visuals": [
    {
      "id": "fig_01",
      "type": "study_design_svg",
      "title": "string — short CONSORT caption (≤40 chars)",
      "layout": "TB",
      "nodes": [
        {"id": "n0", "label": "Total enrolled", "sublabel": null, "n": <total_N>},
        {"id": "n1", "label": "<arm1_short_name>", "sublabel": "received <arm1_treatment>", "n": <arm1_n>},
        {"id": "n2", "label": "<arm2_short_name>", "sublabel": "received <arm2_treatment>", "n": <arm2_n>}
      ],
      "edges": [
        {"from": "n0", "to": "n1", "label": "Randomized"},
        {"from": "n0", "to": "n2", "label": "Randomized"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "chart_01",
      "type": "chartjs",
      "title": "string — outcome name and timeframe",
      "chartType": "bar",
      "labels": ["<arm1_name>", "<arm2_name>"],
      "datasets": [
        {"label": "<arm1_name>", "data": [<arm1_result_value>]},
        {"label": "<arm2_name>", "data": [<arm2_result_value>]}
      ],
      "xLabel": null,
      "yLabel": "string — unit of measurement",
      "units": "string — e.g. months, %, score"
    }
  ],
  "placement": [
    {
      "visualId": "fig_01",
      "insertAfterSection": "What happened in the study?"
    },
    {
      "visualId": "chart_01",
      "insertAfterSection": "What were the main findings from the study?"
    }
  ]
}
